{
  "dom_id": "step-q339969",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Given that $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{\\sqrt{5}}+7$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$ \n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+3{x}^{\\sqrt{5}}+7) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{x})+(\\sqrt{5}\\,{x}^{\\sqrt{5}-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}+\\sqrt{5}\\,{x}^{\\sqrt{5}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
